# Drafted by Gemini (side quests act 2 batch 1: quack), edited.

~ morgan_ask
Narrator: Herb-stained parchment hangs crookedly from the apothecary door, smelling of mint.
morgan [weary]: A pedlar in the Round is selling a plague cure. I cannot leave the kettle, so please see what is in it and whether it does harm.
* We will look into it -> morgan_accept
* Not now -> END

~ morgan_accept
Narrator: You fold the note into your coat while the pestle keeps up its tired rhythm inside.
quest the_quack asked
set quack_asked
-> END

~ pitch
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: Fortify your humours with Pennywhistle's Sovereign Specific! Every green bottle is guaranteed against the creeping itch, or your brass cheerfully refunded.
* Ask what is in it -> ask
* Buy a bottle (two gold) -> buy
* Leave -> END

~ ask
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: I cannot hand over my grandmother's receipt here. Call it forty mountain herbs steeped under a lucky star.
-> pitch

~ buy
gold -2
set quack_bottle
Narrator: The cork pops, releasing a warm waft of cellar cider and cheap cinnamon.
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: A wise investment for troubled times, friend, and do remember to shake the sediment before supper.
-> pitch

~ verdict
Narrator: Barnaby straightens his cuffs by the clinking bottles, watching the crowd with restless eyes.
* [if flag.quack_bottle] [Nature DC 11] Taste the bottle properly -> id_ok | id_off
* Buy a bottle for two gold -> buy_again
* Press Barnaby for the truth -> press

~ id_ok
Narrator: Beneath the cider and cinnamon sits boiled willow and honey. It will cure no plague, only soothe a throat and warm a belly.
set quack_known
-> END

~ id_off
Narrator: Fierce cinnamon and sour apples burn your tongue, masking whatever floats at the bottom.
-> END

~ press
barnaby_pennywhistle [neutral]: You have a terribly solemn look about you, traveller, and solemnity is dreadful for the digestion.
* [Intimidation DC 12] Press Barnaby -> press_ok | press_fail

~ press_ok
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: Keep your voice down before the sick folk lose their temper. It is mulled cider, willow bark for aches, and honey for their spirits.
set quack_known
-> END

~ press_fail
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: I have sold hair tonic to louder bailiffs in three counties. Take two bottles for three coins and spare us the frown.
-> verdict

~ settle
barnaby_pennywhistle [weary]: Warmth and willow tea beat cold panic. What do you mean to do with me?
* Expose him to the village -> expose
* Let him be, but take a bottle for Morgan -> be
* [Persuasion DC 12] Become his partner for a cut -> partner_ok | partner_fail

~ expose
Narrator: Word travels fast, and soon coughing townsfolk are pelting Barnaby's cart toward the gate with turnip tops.
barnaby_pennywhistle [afraid]: Ungrateful hamlet, upon my word! May your joints stay draughty and your tea go cold!
set quack_outcome = "exposed"
quest the_quack done
gold +10
-> END

~ be
barnaby_pennywhistle [smile]: Take the bottom-row bottle for the apothecary, friend, and this coin for a quiet tongue.
set quack_outcome = "left"
quest the_quack done
gold +5
-> END

~ partner_ok
barnaby_pennywhistle [sly]: Stand by the crate looking healthy, nod at the forty herbs, and we shall split the evening's tin.
set quack_outcome = "partner"
quest the_quack done
gold +20
-> END

~ partner_fail
barnaby_pennywhistle [neutral]: No offence, colleague, but a secret shared with four strangers is just a recipe on a tavern wall.
-> settle

~ buy_again
gold -2
set quack_bottle
Narrator: The bottle smells of cider and cinnamon.
-> verdict
